			<section>
				<h2 id="scale-and-notation">Scale and Notation</h2>
				<p>
					These are the basic notes for the gralla and flabiol. For the
					fingering diagrams, a black circle represents a covered hole (put your
					finger down), and a white circle represents an open cole (lift your
					finger up). The topmost circle represents the thumb hold on the bottom
					of the instrument.
				</p>
				<img
					src="/castells-music/sheet music/basic scale/basic scale [solfege, diagrams].svg"
					alt="Sheet music for the basic gralla Scale"
				/>
				<p>
					Note: &nbsp This is not written to concert pitch! This means that the
					'c' or 'do' on your instrument might not be the same as one on a
					different instrument.
				</p>
			</section>

